<p>The FBI is investigating whether Joe Kent, until Tuesday the director of the US National Counterterrorism Center, improperly disclosed classified information, according to multiple outlets citing people familiar with the inquiry. The investigation began before Kent resigned, but his departure quickly drew wider attention after he told President Trump he could not support the ongoing war in Iran and argued that Iran posed no imminent threat to the United States. That overlap — between a leak inquiry and Kent’s public break with administration policy — has turned his resignation into a broader story about internal dissent during a wartime moment. Public reporting does not show that prosecutors have filed charges, and the details described by the FBI and Justice Department remain limited, leaving the central allegations unproven as the inquiry continues.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/aEKbxUec-E1vKGmkpxyvY63cXUxiPGrMmDN-zASdii6vJ47wgXCk79s-Zr_6ON2aPcLrGSGgFOqvLXkUusaPHtDOJd_tzsHEVveazisDDikMbLIJggSrJPed9hUeY5LEhSfNqAMq4OgI-H8yVskPNJaBk7o-LDF6MdqDHTOYjqG73wFbA5cbL2VnnwEUm9-NS7PxcblQ7abk25niVM10T0Hyqa0dZAY_ehCzyVXiJGmVv1vjO-XFCAiv' alt='Joseph Kent appears before a Senate Committee on Intelligence hearing for his pending confirmation to be director of the National Counterterrorism Center, on Capitol Hill, April 9, 2025, in Washington.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Reporting basis: The Semafor report summarized by AllSides said four people with direct knowledge described the investigation, while SCMP cited one person familiar with the matter, so the story currently rests on confidential sourcing.</li><li>Political backdrop: The Hindu reported that the case arrives amid multiple Justice Department investigations over the past year involving political foes of President Trump, which adds to scrutiny over how Washington will view the inquiry.</li><li>Role importance: As head of the National Counterterrorism Center, Kent held a senior post in the US counterterrorism and intelligence system, making any alleged mishandling of classified information especially sensitive.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Joe Kent: In his resignation letter to President Trump, Kent said he could not &#x27;in good conscience&#x27; support the war in Iran, framing his departure as a matter of principle rather than routine turnover. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/19/fbi-probing-counterterrorism-official-who-quit-over-iran-war-us-media-reports_6751597_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>People familiar with the inquiry: SCMP said its source spoke on condition of anonymity because the FBI matter is ongoing, underscoring how preliminary the public account remains. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3347098/fbi-investigating-top-us-security-official-who-resigned-over-iran-war'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Trump allies and pro-Israel commentators: RT reported that some voices quickly cast Kent as a &#x27;known leaker&#x27; and even a suspected anti-Semite, showing how quickly the case took on an ideological edge. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/635535-kent-resignation-fbi-investigation/'>RT</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/19/fbi-probing-counterterrorism-official-who-quit-over-iran-war-us-media-reports_6751597_4.html'>FBI probing counterterrorism official who quit over Iran war, US media reports</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/fbi-investigating-whether-departed-us-counterterrorism-official-joe-kent-leaked-classified-info/article70760523.ece'>FBI investigating whether departed U.S. counterterrorism official Joe Kent leaked classified info</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/03/19/dlkx-m19.html'>Top US intelligence official resigns over Iran war</a> - wsws.org</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/635535-kent-resignation-fbi-investigation/'>Why is the FBI investigating a former counterterrorism chief who opposes the US-Israeli war on Iran?</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3347098/fbi-investigating-top-us-security-official-who-resigned-over-iran-war'>FBI ‘investigating’ top US security official who resigned over Iran war</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c33j3gxvgmro'>Former counter-terrorism head investigated by FBI over alleged leaks</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-19-0700/politics-exclusive-fbi-investigates-intelligence-aide-who-resigned-over-war'>Exclusive / FBI investigates intelligence aide who resigned over war</a> - allsides.com</li></ul>